&Q000514

{1 = 1-10}
9=1.	May Lord @wDN{Nanna}, king of heaven and earth, your good protective deity, 
13=2.	accept the holy food offerings that you prepare, 
17=3.	and the holy pure drink offerings that you proffer with holy hands; 
21=4.	the sacrifices that you bring, what you say in your heart, 
25=5.	what you utter out loud, 
29=6.	your reverent gestures and your holy hands raised in prayer. 
33=7.	May the august queen @wDN{Ningal}, your queen of favourable signs, accept them also. 
37=8.	O king, they who have suppressed famine, the great gods @wDN{Nanna} and @wDN{Ningal}, 
41=9.	have conferred abundance on you, King @wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, 
45=10.	in the temple of the gods. 

{11 = 11-21}
49=11.	O king named with a name by @wDN{Enlil}, the destiny of whose reign is abundance, 
53=12.	a time of richness and years of happiness! 
57=13.	May a destiny of stability and a destiny of abundance be your lot. 
61=14.	O king, day and night, even at dead of night, 
65=15.	time shall pass for you in endless abundance, 
69=16.	and be agreeable and stable for you. O king, 
73=17.	since you have offered your food offerings first offered in the @fsux{abzu}; 
77=18.	O king, since you have offered your food offerings afterwards in the great courtyard, 
81=19.	there shall be no end to the abundance. 
85=20.	O king, the temple shall be well-organised for you. 
89=21.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, king of @wSN{Urim}, has restored the august divine powers of the @wTN{Ki-ur}. 

{22 = 22-38}
93=22.	May @wDN{Nanna}, the king of heaven and earth, fit perfectly onto your head the legitimate august headdress of kingship. 
97=23.	May the august queen @wDN{Ningal}, 
101=24.	who has saved you from famine thanks to her benignity, 
105=25.	let you live (?) an agreeable life for these days. 
109=26.	As you receive from her holy hands the great splendour of kingship, 
113=27.	may she place the august sceptre of heaven and earth in your hands like a ceremonial robe. 
117=28.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, king of the @wTN{Ki-ur}, endowed with abundance, constant attendant! 
121=29.	O king, may the @wWN{Tigris} bring you abundance, 
125=30.	and may the upper (?) @wWN{Nun} canal be filled for you with flowing water in its full flood. 
129=31.	May the @wWN{Nun} canal, the good @wWN{Nun} canal, the life-bringing canal of the Land, 
133=32.	bring you fish and fowl; from the ocean, the wide sea, 
137=33.	from the standing reservoirs, 
141=34.	may it bring an unending supply of creatures for your kingship. 
145=35.	In the wide open spaces of the wide desert, 
149=36.	the four-footed animals ……. 
153=37.	May water levels rise for you in the irrigation ditches, 
157=38.	with their levees, and the water-channels. 

{39 = 39-51}
161=39.	May there be life for you, and may there be a favourable response to your prayers. 
165=40.	May there be joy for you, 
169=41.	and may there be favourable signs for you. 
173=42.	May your heart be satisfied, may your body be satisfied; 
177=43.	may your mood and your definite signs from the gods be good. 
181=44.	May there be favourable omens in the heart of @wDN{Nanna} and @wDN{Ningal}, 
185=45.	and a destiny of life be granted for ever. 
189=46.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, seemly king, who holds abundance in his hands from the great gods, 
193=47.	may the country be stable for you, 
197=48.	and may the foundations of the country be secure for you. 
201=49.	May @wDN{Nanna}, king of heaven and earth, 
205=50.	cause the Land to respond to you with a single voice. 
209=51.	@wRN{Rīm-@wDN{Sîn}}, you are my king! 
